INT. SALOON DURING A THUNDERSTORM - NIGHT

Lamplight. Rain drumming on the tin roof. Poker chips. A cracked mirror behind the bar.

BARNABY "BARN" COLE, 40s, bartender, polishes a glass. SUNNY WELLS, 20s, deals cards in the corner. REVEREND THOMAS GRIGG, 60s, nurses a whiskey. MERCEDES SOTO, 30s, in a duster, sits alone, a rifle across her knees. Two cowhands, JED and PIKE, 20s, play with Sunny.

JED
Barn, another round.

BARN
Jed, you're drunk.

JED
I'm thirsty.

PIKE
Same thing, Jed.

REVEREND GRIGG
Gentlemen, the Lord watches.

JED
The Lord can watch me pay.

Mercedes lifts her head. She watches Jed's hand. Jed's hand moves to his gun.

MERCEDES
Jed Hawkins.

JED
Who's asking?

MERCEDES
Mercedes Soto. You killed my brother in Tucson.

Silence. Lightning. Pike pushes back from the table. Sunny drops the deck. Barn slowly sets down the glass.

BARN
Ma'am. Not in my bar.

MERCEDES
Barn, step aside.

Jed draws. Mercedes fires first. Jed drops, clutching his arm. Pike dives behind the table. Sunny scrambles under it. The Reverend crosses himself and kneels.

BARN
Everybody stay down!

REVEREND GRIGG
Lord, forgive us!

Mercedes stands over Jed, rifle on his chest. Thunder shakes the roof.

JED
(through his teeth)
He pulled first.

MERCEDES
My brother never pulled first in his life.

Barn raises his hands. Pike peeks up. Sunny crawls out. The Reverend rises and walks to Jed's side, kneels.

REVEREND GRIGG
Miss Soto, let me tend him.

MERCEDES
Reverend, he's yours.

She lowers the rifle, turns, and walks out into the rain.
